IMPORT prelude

-- Development Fund Act 1959 (Singapore) -- the whole Act: the saving for expenditure before 14 September 1959 (s 1(2)), what is paid
-- into the Development Fund (s 2), what the Fund may be spent on and the Schedule of purposes (s 3, Schedule), the warrant and the
-- transfer between subheads of one head (s 4), the ring-fence on money borrowed under the Significant Infrastructure Government Loan
-- Act 2021 (s 5), and advances from the Contingencies Fund (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DFA1959.txt. The deposit says
-- the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021";
-- its page footer reads "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 5/12/2025". The latest amendment annotated in the text is
-- Act 19 of 2025 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2025) "wef 05/12/2025", which inserted s 6(2A) and amended s 6(3); Act 3
-- of 2024 (wef 26 February 2024) amended ss 4 and 6(2). The source metadata records the version as current at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0166 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The honest answer is: almost nothing directly. The Act is a public-finance statute addressed to the Minister, the
-- President and Parliament. A person or business meets it only at the edges: as the recipient of a grant or loan from the Fund
-- (Schedule para 6, "any other corporation or body"), as a seller of land or of the use of an invention (para 2), and as a borrower
-- whose repayments go into the Fund (s 2(f)). The Act is short (ss 1-6 and one Schedule), so the scope is all of it.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the long title and s 1(1); what counts as a "Supply or Supplementary Supply law" or as "nationally significant
-- infrastructure expenditure within the meaning of section 11" of the 2021 Act (that Act was not read); the meanings of "capital
-- contribution" and "statutory corporation" borrowed from s 7A of the Financial Procedure Act 1966 (Schedule para 7(2)); the terms
-- the Minister for Finance may set for a capital injection; and the investment of Fund moneys (s 2(e) assumes another law authorises
-- it). The Act creates no offence, no penalty and no right of action.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example rows (the writing-l4-rules skill was not
-- available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Development Fund Act 1959 -- the Fund`

§§ `1(2) -- expenditure before 14 September 1959`

-- s 1(2): "Nothing in this Act shall be deemed to affect the legality of any expenditure incurred before 14 September 1959."
-- (14 September 1959 is also the commencement date in the long title and the Legislative History.)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER, month IS A NUMBER, day IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is on or after 14 September 1959` IF
        year GREATER THAN 1959
    OR  (year EQUALS 1959 AND (month GREATER THAN 9 OR (month EQUALS 9 AND day AT LEAST 14)))

GIVEN year IS A NUMBER, month IS A NUMBER, day IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act can affect the legality of expenditure incurred on` IF
    `is on or after 14 September 1959` year month day

§§ `2 -- what is paid into the Development Fund`

-- s 2: "There shall be in and for Singapore a Development Fund into which, subject to the provisions of any other written law, shall be
-- paid -- (a) all moneys from time to time appropriated and authorised to be paid into the Development Fund by this Act or by any other
-- written law; (b) all sums representing the proceeds of any loan raised by Singapore for the purposes of the Development Fund and
-- appropriated to such purposes by the law authorising the raising of the loan; (c) all loans or grants from time to time made to
-- Singapore for the purposes of or properly allocable to the Development Fund; (d) all revenues of Singapore allocated to the
-- Development Fund; (e) all interest on investments of moneys in the Development Fund authorised to be made by this Act or by any
-- other written law, and all profits arising from the realisation of any such investments; and (f) all sums representing repayments of
-- any loans made from the Development Fund, or payments of interest on such loans."
--
-- Each head except (a) and (f) carries a condition of its own, which the caller states as `its own condition is met`:
-- (b) raised for the Fund AND appropriated to it by the loan law; (c) for the purposes of, or properly allocable to, the Fund;
-- (d) allocated to the Fund; (e) the investment was authorised by this Act or another written law. For (a) and (f) the condition is
-- part of the description and the flag is ignored.
DECLARE Receipt IS ONE OF
    `money appropriated to the Fund by written law`
    `proceeds of a loan raised by Singapore`
    `a loan or grant made to Singapore`
    `revenue of Singapore`
    `interest or profit on an investment of Fund money`
    `repayment of, or interest on, a loan made from the Fund`

GIVEN `the receipt` IS A Receipt, `its own condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN, `another written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is paid into the Development Fund` IF
        (NOT `another written law provides otherwise`)
    AND CONSIDER `the receipt`
        WHEN `money appropriated to the Fund by written law` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `repayment of, or interest on, a loan made from the Fund` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `its own condition is met`

§§ `3, 5 and the Schedule -- what the Fund may be spent on`

-- s 3: "Subject to section 5, the moneys in the Development Fund shall be applied only to the purposes or any one or more thereof
-- specified in the Schedule and in accordance with a Supply or Supplementary Supply law appropriating and directing the expenditure of
-- such moneys."
--
-- The Schedule, "Purposes to which the Development Fund may be applied":
-- 1. "The construction, improvement, extension, enlargement and replacement of buildings and works and the provision, acquisition,
--    improvement and replacement of other capital assets (including vehicles, vessels, aircraft, rolling-stock, machinery, instruments
--    and equipment) required in respect of or in connection with the economic development or general welfare of Singapore."
-- 2. "The acquisition of land and of any right or interest in or over land and in respect of the use of any invention."
-- 3. "The carrying on of any survey, research or investigation preparatory to the undertaking of any such purpose as is referred to in
--    paragraph 1 or to the formation of any plan or scheme for the development, improvement, conservation or exploitation of the
--    resources of Singapore or of any part thereof."
-- 4. Charges or expenses incidental to or arising from paragraphs 1, 2 and 3.
-- 5. Charges or expenses incidental to or arising out of "depreciation or losses on investments of moneys in the Development Fund".
-- 6. "Grants and loans to any public authority, or any other corporation or body, for any one or more of the purposes referred to in
--    paragraphs 1 to 4." -- NOT paragraphs 5 or 7.
-- 7.(1) "Capital contribution for investment by way of capital injection in any statutory corporation" on terms the Minister for
--    Finance determines after consulting the Minister in charge, or as prescribed by written law.
--
-- The last three members of Purpose below are not in the Schedule. That salaries, running costs and cash payments to households are
-- outside it is the encoding's reading of the Schedule's words (all of which are capital, land, survey or investment purposes); the
-- Act does not name them.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `a building, works or other capital asset`
    `acquiring land or a right over land`
    `paying for the use of an invention`
    `a survey or research preparatory to paragraph 1 or a resource plan`
    `charges incidental to paragraphs 1 to 3`
    `charges arising from depreciation or losses on Fund investments`
    `a grant or loan to a body for paragraphs 1 to 4`
    `a capital injection into a statutory corporation`
    `a grant or loan to a body for any other purpose`
    `salaries and running costs`
    `cash payments to households`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `connected with Singapore's development or welfare` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a purpose in the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `a building, works or other capital asset` THEN `connected with Singapore's development or welfare`
    WHEN `acquiring land or a right over land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paying for the use of an invention` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a survey or research preparatory to paragraph 1 or a resource plan` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `charges incidental to paragraphs 1 to 3` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `charges arising from depreciation or losses on Fund investments` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a grant or loan to a body for paragraphs 1 to 4` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a capital injection into a statutory corporation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 5(1): "All sums borrowed under the Significant Infrastructure Government Loan Act 2021 and which are paid into the Development Fund
-- may be applied only to meet nationally significant infrastructure expenditure within the meaning of section 11 of that Act."
-- (2): "To avoid doubt, subsection (1) does not prevent authorising the issue of any sum from the Development Fund and applying the money
-- to meet an estimate of any nationally significant infrastructure expenditure ... on a provisional basis."
--
-- FORK. s 3 is "subject to section 5". The encoding reads that as: for money borrowed under the 2021 Act, s 5's test (nationally
-- significant infrastructure, actual or a provisional estimate) takes the place of the Schedule. The other reading is that such money
-- must satisfy both. The two differ only for infrastructure that falls outside every Schedule paragraph, which seems unlikely given
-- paragraph 1's breadth (an inference). Both readings still require a Supply or Supplementary Supply law.
DECLARE `Proposed spending`
    HAS `the purpose of the spending` IS A Purpose
        `is connected with Singapore's development or welfare` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is appropriated by a Supply or Supplementary Supply law` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is money borrowed under the 2021 Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is nationally significant infrastructure expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is a provisional estimate of such expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the spending` IS A `Proposed spending`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may be applied to it` IF
        `the spending`'s `is appropriated by a Supply or Supplementary Supply law`
    AND (IF `the spending`'s `is money borrowed under the 2021 Loan Act`
         THEN `the spending`'s `is nationally significant infrastructure expenditure`
              OR `the spending`'s `is a provisional estimate of such expenditure`
         ELSE `is a purpose in the Schedule` (`the spending`'s `the purpose of the spending`) (`the spending`'s `is connected with Singapore's development or welfare`))

§§ `4 -- the warrant, and moving money between subheads`

-- s 4(1): "The Minister may, by warrant, authorise the issue of any sum from the Development Fund to meet expenditure appropriated by a
-- Supply or Supplementary Supply law."
GIVEN `there is a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN, `the expenditure is appropriated by a Supply law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a sum may issue from the Fund` IF
    `there is a warrant` AND `the expenditure is appropriated by a Supply law`

-- s 4(2): if it appears to the Minister "necessary to alter the proportion assigned to any of the subheads of any head of expenditure
-- ... or to create a new subhead, the Minister may, by warrant, authorise the transfer of a further sum out of any surplus arising on any
-- other subhead of the same head, in aid of any subhead which may be deficient or of any new subhead except that the amount appropriated
-- under any head of expenditure ... shall not be thereby exceeded."
--
-- Because the money must come out of a SURPLUS on another subhead of the SAME head, a transfer within that surplus cannot take the head
-- above its appropriation (the encoding's arithmetic, not words of the Act). Nothing can be moved from one head to another.
GIVEN `from the same head` IS A BOOLEAN, `surplus on the other subhead` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be transferred` MEANS
    IF `from the same head` THEN `surplus on the other subhead` ELSE 0

GIVEN `by warrant` IS A BOOLEAN, `from the same head` IS A BOOLEAN, `the receiving subhead is deficient or new` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `surplus on the other subhead` IS A NUMBER, `the sum to move` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer may be authorised` IF
        `by warrant`
    AND `the receiving subhead is deficient or new`
    AND `the sum to move` AT MOST `the most that may be transferred` `from the same head` `surplus on the other subhead`

§§ `6 -- the Contingencies Fund`

-- s 6(1): "A Contingencies Fund is hereby created consisting of moneys from time to time appropriated thereto from the Development Fund."
-- (2): the Minister may make advances from it "if he is satisfied that there has arisen an urgent and unforeseen need for expenditure for
-- which no other provision exists and for which funds cannot be provided under section 4(2), and if the President, acting in his
-- discretion, concurs with the making of an advance for such need".
-- (2A): "An advance under subsection (2) must be authorised by a warrant issued under the authority of the Minister." [Act 19 of 2025]
-- (3): a supplementary estimate of the sum required to replace the advance "shall, as soon as practicable, be presented to and voted on
-- by Parliament and the sum shall be included in a Supplementary Supply or Final Supply law".
DECLARE `Proposed advance`
    HAS `the need is urgent` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the need is unforeseen` IS A BOOLEAN
        `no other provision exists` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a s 4(2) transfer could meet it` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the President concurs` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a Minister's warrant authorises it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the advance` IS A `Proposed advance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advance may be made` IF
        `the advance`'s `the need is urgent`
    AND `the advance`'s `the need is unforeseen`
    AND `the advance`'s `no other provision exists`
    AND (NOT `the advance`'s `a s 4(2) transfer could meet it`)
    AND `the advance`'s `the President concurs`
    AND `the advance`'s `a Minister's warrant authorises it`

GIVEN `an advance was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parliament must vote a supplementary estimate to replace it` IF
    `an advance was made`
